@startuml 05-rastok-packages
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty methods
top to bottom direction
title Rastok — current core data forms (registry: identity.md)

package "envelope" {
  class Envelope {
    meta: Meta
    data: Data
  }
  class Meta {
    sys: MetaSys
    app / ext: metadata
  }
  class MetaSys {
    id: Id
    parent_id: Option<Id>
    origin_id: Id
    graph_version: u64
  }
  enum Data {
    Encoded { encoding, bytes, value_cache }
    Materialized(Value)
  }
  enum Encoding {
    Raw
    Ccbor
    ArrowIpc
  }
  class Delivery {
    edge: EdgeIndex
    seq: u64
    source_instance: instance::Generation
    envelope: Envelope
  }
}

package "instance / node" {
  class "instance::InstanceSpec" as Spec {
    key: Option<expr::Tree>
    lifetime: Lifetime
    closing: Option<Closing>
  }
  class "instance::InstanceAddress" as Identity {
    scope: Arc<node::OwnerPath>
    bytes: Arc<[u8]>
  }
  enum "instance::Segment" as Segment {
    SelectedKey
    ProcessingTimeBox
  }
  class "instance::Generation" as Generation {
    address: InstanceAddress
    generation: u64
  }
  class "instance::LiveInstance" as Live {
    ephemeral lifecycle / admission state
    residual: Vec<Delivery>
    crate-private; not journal authority
  }
}

package "journal" {
  enum Record {
    Ingress(Box<IngressRecord>)
    Transaction(Box<TransactionRecord>)
    Egress(EgressRecord)
  }
  class IngressRecord {
    envelope / source / sequence / ingress port
    routes / instance commands / inbound exchange
    unsealed deadlines
  }
  class TransactionRecord {
    owner / instance / trigger / consumed positions
    state delta / ordered emissions / routes
    deadline ids / Loop / Retry / closure facts
    observed_time: Option<Timestamp>
    unsealed deadlines
  }
  enum EgressRecord {
    Call(Box<CallRecord>)
    Session(Box<SessionRecord>)
  }
  class CallRecord {
    intent / status / Retry context
    unsealed closed_at / deadlines
  }
  class SessionRecord {
    connector_path / session_id / status
  }
  class "deadline::Deadlines" as Deadlines {
    created_at: LogicalTime
    items: Vec<Deadline>
  }
  class "deadline::Deadline" as Deadline {
    kind: DeadlineKind
    reference: Id
    due_at: LogicalTime
  }
}

package "canonical encoding" {
  class "canonical" as CANONICAL <<module>> {
    envelope / data / value / meta_value
    shared tag registry
  }
  class "canonical_cbor" as CBOR <<module>> {
    bounded canonical byte discipline
    no journal or value tag registry
  }
  class "journal::codec" as CODEC <<module>> {
    encode / Decoder
    lossless records, including unsealed fields
  }
}

Envelope *-- Meta
Envelope *-- Data
Meta *-- MetaSys
Data --> Encoding
Delivery *-- Envelope
Delivery --> Generation
Identity ..> Segment : encodes
Generation *-- Identity
Live --> Generation
Live *-- Delivery
Record *-- IngressRecord
Record *-- TransactionRecord
Record *-- EgressRecord
IngressRecord --> Envelope
TransactionRecord --> Envelope : ordered emissions
TransactionRecord --> Generation
EgressRecord *-- CallRecord
EgressRecord *-- SessionRecord
IngressRecord --> Deadlines
TransactionRecord --> Deadlines
CallRecord --> Deadlines
Deadlines *-- Deadline
CANONICAL --> CBOR
CODEC --> CANONICAL
CODEC ..> Record

note bottom of Data
Encoded bytes share Arc<[u8]>; the lazy cache is not identity.
Graph-born values use canonical CBOR. Raw bytes stay external;
the reader's port type selects bytes or checked UTF-8 text.
end note
note bottom of Delivery
EdgeIndex is local to one Execution, not a journal identity.
DeliveryRoutes resolves its arrival port and canonical cursor path.
Journal records keep paths and exact instance generations.
end note
note bottom of Record
Three append-only kinds: INGRESS, TRANSACTION, EGRESS.
An EGRESS Call opens then closes in separate records.
Unsealed instants are required recovery evidence, not causal seal input.
LogicalTime counts nanoseconds from logical zero, not the Unix epoch.
The unsealed journal header retains the immutable civil origin.
An observed now() seals origin + LogicalTime as a civil Timestamp pair.
end note

legend bottom
Owned types and selected fields, not an exhaustive API inventory.
All boxes are in rastok-core (no_std + alloc).
The current format and allocated numbers live in docs/spec/identity.md.
endlegend
@enduml
